        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70839,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours arise within the epididymis and may involve the paratesticular tissues.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70840,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The symptoms include a scrotal mass, hydrocoele, and pain {13809911; 8372688; 32619438}. The duration of reported symptoms ranged from 1&nbsp;month to 5&nbsp;years {5391157; 9801128}. No bilaterality or side predilection has been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70841,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epididymal adenocarcinoma represents only 2% of all testicular appendage tumours {32619438}. The patient age range is 24&ndash;82&nbsp;years (mean: 55&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70842,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70843,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70844,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are grey-white and firm with necrosis and haemorrhage. Cystic areas may be present. The size ranges from 20&nbsp;to 140&nbsp;mm {9414191; 1729518}. Large tumours can involve the surrounding structures.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70845,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The morphological patterns are tubular, papillary, tubulopapillary, papillary cystic, and undifferentiated sheet-like growth. The tubules and papillae are lined by cuboidal to columnar cells with clear to amphophilic cytoplasm {9414191}. A single case of mucinous differentiation has been reported {25839701}. A clear cell pattern may be present {23348385}. Stromal invasion, necrosis, and psammoma bodies have been observed {9414191}. Immunohistochemistry is positive for EMA, CEA, PAX8, PAX2, and villin. Tumours with mucinous and clear cell differentiation express CK20 and CK7 {25839701; 23348385}. Immunohistochemistry is negative for WT1, CDX2, AMACR, PSA, and RCCm. The differential diagnosis includes mesothelioma, ovarian-type serous or mucinous cystadenocarcinoma, adenocarcinoma of the rete testis, and metastatic adenocarcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
