  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70848,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> epididymal location; malignant cytomorphological features; glandular differentiation; infiltrative growth; exclusion of rete testis carcinoma, ovarian-type tumours, mesothelioma, and metastatic adenocarcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70849,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging system for this tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70850,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Due to the scarcity of reported cases, the prognostic factors remain uncertain. Radical orchiectomy with retroperitoneal lymphadenectomy, irrespective of lymph node status, is suggested to achieve relapse-free survival {22382506}. Cases in which retroperitoneal lymph node metastasis is found at the time of diagnosis may have a better prognosis than those in which metastasis develops after retroperitoneal lymph node dissection {29423406}. Distant metastases (paraurethral tissue {1729518}, acetabulum, spleen, and liver {15338681}) are associated with a poor prognosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]